.Dd 2026-11-07
.Dt LBTS-FSCK 1
.\" Manual page created by:
.\" Guus Sliepen <guus@lightbts.info>
.Sh NAME
.Nm lbts fsck
.Nd check the messages and the index for problems
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm lbts fsck
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The command checks a LightBTS instance for problems, without changing anything.
It reports:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Message files that cannot be indexed,
for example because they are not valid messages,
or because they are not stored under the name that their Message-ID determines.
These have to be fixed or removed by hand.
.It
Problems found by SQLite's own integrity checks of the index,
including references to tickets that do not exist.
.It
Differences between the index and what rebuilding it from the messages would produce,
for example messages that are not in the index,
messages in the index whose file is missing,
tickets whose fields or links differ,
and an index that was built with other field definitions.
.El
.Pp
The last two kinds of problems are fixed by running
.Nm lbts reindex .
In fact,
.Nm lbts fsck
finds the differences by rebuilding the index inside a transaction that is then rolled back,
so it reports exactly what
.Nm lbts reindex
would change.
.Pp
Unlike other commands,
.Nm lbts fsck
does not rebuild an index that was built with other field definitions,
but reports it.
.Pp
Problems are printed on stdout, one per line,
prefixed with "Message file:", "Database:" or "Index:".
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The command exits with status 0 if no problems were found, and with status 1 otherwise.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr lbts 1 ,
.Xr lbts-reindex 1 .
.Sh AUTHOR
.An "Guus Sliepen" Aq guus@lightbts.info
